        A monthly temperature normal is a 30-year average of monthly temperature data collected during a specific month at a specific geographic location. The table below presents the monthly temperature normals (°F) in July for six climate divisions in the U.S.<fn>https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access</fn>
      </p>
